    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>An <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oirats">Oirat</a> Mongol khanate founded in the 1630s in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungaria">Dzungaria</a> and the Ili valley under the Choros dynasty.</li><li>It conquered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarim-basin">Tarim Basin</a>, sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lhasa">Lhasa</a> in 1717 and devastated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazakhs">Kazakh</a> steppe, contesting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> with the Qing.</li><li>After succession wars, Qing armies destroyed it in 1755–1758 in a campaign many historians call a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungars">Dzungars</a> cast <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/field-artillery">cannon</a> with the help of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johan-gustaf-renat">Johan Gustaf Renat</a>, a Swedish officer captured by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-poltava">Poltava</a> in 1709 who later fell into Dzungar hands.</p></aside>
    </section>

